1:# Phase 1 Plan: Investment Copilot (read-only)
5:Sections: decisions, migrations, jobs, tool surface, journal builder, stops and open risk, snapshots, UI, testing, deploy, build order, deferred items, Schwab assumptions, working method.
9:## 0. Decisions (resolved 2026-09-01)
13:3. **Web login is passwordless magic link**, built on the Rails 8 auth generator with `generates_token_for :magic_link` (15 min, single use). Users are seeded, not self-registered: john@athayde.com and whitney@athayde.com only. No gem. Because a second person can log in, `audit_events.user_id` exists from day one so Phase 2 approvals are attributable. Fallback when email is down: `bin/rails login:link[email]` prints a magic link to the console.
14:4. **Email via Resend over SMTP**, no gem; API key in credentials. Production login and re-auth depend on it, so Resend DNS is a prerequisite for the first production deploy.
18:8. **MCP auth (open verification, not blocking):** the Claude app's custom-connector UI exposes static bearer headers only to orgs in a beta. John checks Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector for a "headers" option before step 8. If absent, the fallback is a minimal OAuth 2.1 authorization-code + PKCE endpoint on the app that issues the same bearer after magic-link login. `McpAuth` verifies the bearer either way, so the tool layer is unaffected.
22:## 1. Migrations (in creation order)
46:| 19 | `agent_runs` | `kind` enum (morning_brief, eod, sunday_review), `status`, `degraded` bool (ran with expired token / stale data), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `tool_turns`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `estimated_cost`, `output_markdown`, `error`, `model` | yes |
48:| 21 | `system_settings` | Singleton row (check constraint `id = 1`): `shadow_mode` bool default true, `manual_halt` bool default false, `manual_halt_reason`, `manual_halt_at`, `sync_paused_reason` (set while token expired) | yes |
56:## 2. Jobs (Solid Queue, `config/recurring.yml`, all times America/New_York)
58:**Token gating.** Only `Sync::TickJob` and the agent jobs are scheduled; everything else is enqueued by them. When the refresh token is expired the tick job writes one `sync_runs` `skipped_token` row per hour, sets `system_settings.sync_paused_reason`, audits `sync_paused_token_expired` once per episode, and enqueues nothing. No self-re-enqueue, so the queue cannot grow. The re-auth callback clears the pause and enqueues `Sync::CatchUpJob`, which runs all feeds with windows widened to cover the gap (capped at the 60-day transactions limit). Agent jobs run degraded rather than wait: `degraded: true`, the prompt states the token is expired and every number carries its as-of time, and the email subject is prefixed accordingly. Snapshots are not written for days without a fresh balance.
62:| `Schwab::RefreshAccessTokenJob` | every 25 min | POST refresh grant; update `schwab_tokens` (`refresh_expires_at` untouched); on failure audit `token_refresh_failed`; no-op when refresh token expired |
63:| `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` | daily 08:00 + 20:00 | Nag when `refresh_expires_at` < now + 24h. Escalation rule: on Monday and Tuesday, email if `refresh_expires_at` is before the coming Sunday 18:00 email plus 12h buffer (Sunday re-auth was missed). Audit each nag. |
65:| `Sync::AccountsJob` | daily 06:05, after every re-auth | `/accounts/accountNumbers` then `/accounts`; upsert by `schwab_hash` |
69:| `Sync::CatchUpJob` | after re-auth | Accounts, positions, orders, transactions with widened windows |
78:| `Agent::SundayReviewJob` | Sunday 18:00 | Phase 1 stub, no API call: re-auth link, token age, sync health, job failures, setup stats table |
84:## 3. Tool surface (one registry, two transports)
92:| `get_quotes(symbols)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/quotes`, cached 2 min in Solid Cache, each quote stamped with fetched_at; when the token is expired returns the cached value with `stale: true` or an explicit unavailable error |
100:**MCP server:** `POST /mcp` (Streamable HTTP, JSON-RPC 2.0). `McpAuth` extracts a bearer from `Authorization` and compares with `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`; 401 renders a plain "MCP auth failed" page (Playwright target). See decision 0.8 for the OAuth fallback.
106:## 4. Journal builder (zero-to-zero, trading-enabled accounts only)
129:## 5. Stops and open risk in Phase 1
139:## 6. Snapshots (per account, chain-linked)
151:## 7. UI (Hotwire, mobile-responsive, no JS routers, no hover-dependent modals)
155:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner (healthy / expiring / expired / halted), equity + day change, open risk with unprotected count, settled/unsettled cash, positions list with distance-to-stop as the primary number and inline `unprotected` where applicable, "N trades need review" callout, pending proposals count (0), staleness stamps on every number, empty state before first sync |
159:| Re-auth | `/schwab/authorize` → Schwab → `/schwab/callback` | Requires login; success page with new expiry and catch-up sync enqueued; failure page with error and retry |
164:Banner precedence: halted > expired > expiring > healthy. Halted in Phase 1 comes only from `system_settings.manual_halt`.
