11:3. **Sunday email** → re-auth link and edge review link.
26:| System health | Mobile + desktop | Token age, sync status, jobs, kill switch |
28:## Flow 1: Morning glance (mobile, read-only)
32:Dashboard states (mutually exclusive banners, one at a time):
33:- **Healthy:** no banner.
34:- **Token expiring:** refresh token < 24h. Banner links to re-auth flow.
35:- **Token expired:** sync paused. Everything shows "as of [timestamp]" staleness marks. Re-auth is the only call to action.
48:2. Thesis: the agent's (or your) one-paragraph reasoning, plus which setup it's tagged as.
70:Submit → same validation path and proposal detail screen as Flow 2. Human and agent proposals are identical objects downstream; the only difference is the author field.
80:## Flow 5: Sunday ritual
82:Sunday email contains: edge review summary, system health summary, re-auth button.
84:- **Re-auth:** button → Schwab OAuth (their hosted login) → callback → success screen showing new token expiry date. Failure state: retry with the error shown.
85:- **Edge review** screen: per-setup table (win rate, avg R, expectancy, sample size, trailing-20 trend). Setups with negative expectancy flagged. Action per setup: deactivate (confirm dialog stating the effect: agent stops proposing this setup). Reactivation same path.
91:No bulk edit. No editing while a halt is active (prevents mood-driven loosening on a bad day; the halt banner says so).
95:List: symbol, trigger note ("break above 52.10 on volume"), added date, current price vs trigger. Add/edit/remove. The agent reads triggers; a trigger being met surfaces in the morning brief, not as a push (v1).
97:## Flow 8: System health & kill switch
99:Token age (days:hours, with the Sunday cadence marked), last successful sync per feed, recent job failures, API spend this month. One control: **Pause system** (kill switch): stops all proposal creation and submission until unpaused. Unpause requires typed confirmation.
104:- **Stale data:** any market number older than its cache window shows a staleness mark with timestamp. Never render a price without its age being discoverable.
105:- **Token expired:** global banner, read-only mode for anything requiring fresh Schwab data.
110:Push (deep-link only, no figures in the payload): new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, unprotected position, token expiring. Email: morning brief, EOD summary, Sunday ritual, job-failure digests. Original list:
116:- Token expiring (T-24h), escalations Mon/Tue if Sunday re-auth missed
117:- Job failure (collapsed: one email per failure type per day)
131:- **Payment confirmation → the deliberate confirm.** Mercury puts an authorization sentence directly above a single primary button ("By clicking Schedule Payment, I authorize…"). That is our Approve pattern: a plain-language line stating exactly what will be sent to Schwab, then one primary button. Given the stakes, keep a second gesture, but model it on this rather than a modal.
140:- **Midday (web) → app shell and dashboard.** Icon-only collapsed left rail (~40px) with a top search bar; dark theme; chart cards with a headline number, legend (current / previous / average), dashed average line, and a timeframe dropdown plus "Customize" at the card row's top right. Layout: one full-width primary chart, then a 2-up row of smaller chart cards. Our mapping: equity curve as the primary chart with HWM as the dashed line; the 2-up row is open risk over time and drawdown from HWM. The rail holds our five areas: dashboard, proposals, journal, watchlist, system.
145:Open interaction with the earlier question: a dark shell makes "halt mutes the whole palette" a weaker signal than on a light UI; the halt banner probably has to carry the state on its own.
152:- **Holding detail page.** Price chart with range chips, a "Your position" strip (balance, shares, cost basis, return, allocation), then a right-column card with News / About tabs and a stats row below. This is our **Position detail** screen, which the inventory above omits. Our version of the strip: shares, cost basis, unrealized P&L, working stop, distance to stop, this position's share of open risk. Right column tabs become Thesis (from the originating proposal) and History (journal legs for this instrument).
172:**Review modal → orphan-fill and incomplete-journal review.** "Is this merchant recurring? There are 9 more to review": entity card with recent transactions, a few form fields, and three actions (Skip / Not recurring / Save as recurring). Ours: "Is this fill part of a setup? N more to review", recent fills for the instrument, setup dropdown and planned stop, actions Skip / Not a trade / Save. The orange top banner with "Review now" is the pending-review entry point; the nav badge count (Recurring 10) is the proposals count on the rail.
180:**AI-origin marker.** Monarch marks AI-generated content with a sparkle glyph next to the title (Weekly Recap, Budget, Spending). Adopt it: every agent-authored element (thesis, brief, review suggestion) carries the glyph, so human vs agent origin is legible at a glance. Ties to the origin field on proposals.

