docs/schwab-api-contract.md:3:Compiled 2026-09-01 from schwab-py, Schwabdev, the sudowealth TypeScript schemas, schwab-client-js, the R `charlesschwabapi` package, and QuantConnect, via the counselors review in `agents/counselors/1788298377-*`. The api-evangelist OpenAPI files are skeletal and are not used for shapes. Nothing here has been confirmed against Schwab's portal; `docs/verify-on-approval.md` lists what to check once the app is Ready For Use. Adapter code marks each assumption `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED`.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:5:Hosts: `https://api.schwabapi.com/trader/v1` and `https://api.schwabapi.com/marketdata/v1`. Every API call sends `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` and `Accept: application/json`. Responses are bare arrays or objects, no envelope.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:15:7. **Retries:** GETs and the refresh grant only, on 429 and 5xx and transport errors; 1, 4, 16 seconds with jitter, `Retry-After` honored but capped at 60 s. Never retry 4xx. One refresh-and-retry on a 401 outside the budget.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:24:| `Schwab::AuthError` | API 401 after the one refresh-and-retry |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:25:| `Schwab::ReauthRequired < AuthError` | any token-endpoint 4xx (`invalid_client`, `invalid_grant`, `refresh_token_authentication_error`, `unsupported_token_type`); the pause path |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:33:Error bodies: API errors are JSON:API style `{"errors":[{"id","status","title","detail","source"}]}`; the token endpoint uses `{"error","error_description"}`; gateway 401s and 5xxs can be non-JSON. The parser tolerates all three.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:35:## OAuth
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:39:| Authorize | `GET /v1/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={app_key}&redirect_uri={callback}&state={csrf}` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:40:| Callback | `{callback}?code=...&session=...`; `code` ends in `@` after one URL-decode. Rails `params[:code]` is already decoded once; do not decode again |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:41:| Token endpoint | `POST /v1/oauth/token`, `Authorization: Basic base64("#{app_key}:#{app_secret}")`, `Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:42:| Code grant | `grant_type=authorization_code&code={code}&redirect_uri={callback}` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:43:| Refresh grant | `grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={token}` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:44:| Token response | `{"expires_in":1800,"token_type":"Bearer","scope":"api","refresh_token","access_token","id_token"}`; `id_token` is not persisted |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:45:| Access token | 30 minutes; expired tokens are rejected outright (API 401) |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:46:| Refresh token | 7 days from the authorization-code grant. **Refreshing does not extend it.** `refresh_expires_at` is set once at issuance and never moved |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:47:| Refresh response | includes a `refresh_token`; store whatever comes back, keep `refresh_expires_at` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:49:The refresh job runs every 25 minutes. A token-endpoint 4xx is `ReauthRequired`: no backoff, no retry, pause sync.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:122:Symbols comma-joined and URL-encoded; chunk at 100. Response keyed by symbol: `assetMainType` (EQUITY|ETF|...), `assetSubType`, `quoteType`, `realtime`, `ssid`, `symbol`, `reference` {cusip, description, exchange, exchangeName}, `quote` {askPrice, bidPrice, lastPrice, mark, netChange, netPercentChange, openPrice, highPrice, lowPrice, closePrice, totalVolume, quoteTime, tradeTime, securityStatus, 52WeekHigh, 52WeekLow}, `regular` {regularMarketLastPrice, ...}. `quoteTime`/`tradeTime` are epoch ms. Unknown symbols return in the same 200 under a top-level `errors` key (`{"errors":{"invalidSymbols":[...]}}`); the mapper skips it and reports the list.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:144:`Schwab::FakeClient` sits **below the mappers**: it returns scrubbed raw hashes in the same shape as the HTTP client, so seeds and Playwright exercise the mapping code where every shape assumption lives, and its fixtures double as the cassette-shaped fixtures for specs. It scripts auth too (`authorize_url`, `exchange_code`, `refresh`) and supports a per-call response queue so a test can say "first `orders` call raises RateLimited, second succeeds". Scenarios: re-auth success and failure, refresh expired, rate limited then success, server error then success, transport timeout, empty account, position removed between syncs, nested bracket child, transaction with missing CUSIP, unknown enum value, closed market day, quotes batch with one invalid symbol, and the four dashboard banner states.

